# Top-level TEST deps for services/ai-backend. Regenerate the lock:
#   cd services/ai-backend && .venv/bin/pip-compile --generate-hashes --resolver=backtracking requirements-dev.in -o requirements-dev.txt
#
# `requirements.in` is the RUNTIME set — what the Docker image (services/
# ai-backend/Dockerfile) and the desktop's bundled runtime install. Test tooling
# does not belong there: it ships nothing, and `pip-audit` plus the CycloneDX
# SBOM step in ci-ai-backend.yml deliberately read `requirements.txt` ALONE so
# they describe only what is actually deployed. Keep those two pointed at the
# runtime file when editing that workflow.
#
# Every CI job that runs pytest installs the compiled `requirements-dev.txt`,
# which pulls the runtime set in via this `-r`. That replaces the ad-hoc
# `pip install pytest` that used to drift per workflow — one unpinned install is
# how a job ended up with pytest but no pytest-asyncio.
-r requirements.in

pytest==9.1.1
pytest-asyncio==1.4.0

# Optional AC6 "Code Mode" interpreter. It is gated OFF at runtime by
# RUNTIME_ENABLE_MONTY and imported lazily behind InterpreterPort, so it is not
# part of the runtime set; the desktop installs it only on explicit opt-in via
# `copilot install --code-mode`, from
# tools/desktop-runtime/features/monty-requirements.txt.
#
# The interpreter suite asserts the port BUILDS rather than skipping when the
# wheel is absent ("Monty is a pinned dependency, so availability holds in this
# suite" — tests/unit/agent_runtime/capabilities/interpreter/test_registration.py),
# so tests need the wheel: without it 30 tests fail on build_monty_interpreter
# returning None.
#
# HELD at 0.0.18. 0.0.19 replaces the in-process `Monty(code).start(...)` /
# `FunctionSnapshot.resume` model that monty_adapter.py is built on with a
# subprocess worker pool: `Monty` is now a context manager whose only method is
# `checkout`, and code reaches the interpreter through `MontySession.feed_start`
# / `feed_run` instead of the constructor. Porting the adapter to that lifecycle
# is a design change to a flag-off capability, not a dependency bump, so it is
# tracked separately. tools/desktop-runtime/features/monty-requirements.txt
# pins 0.0.18 too — both move together or the desktop opt-in installs a wheel
# the adapter cannot drive.
pydantic-monty==0.0.18
